# How a bazzite window is laid out. Read by `workspace up`, and by prefix + w.
# Worktrees of this repo inherit it.
#
# This is `tds` from the dotfiles repo written down as a plan: a guitar in each
# of the six repos this desktop is built out of across a thin top strip, over
# one large atrium.
#
#   +----------+----------+----------+----------+----------+----------+
#   |  guitar  |  guitar  |  guitar  |  guitar  |  guitar  |  guitar  | 20%
#   | bazzite  | dotfiles |   tmux   |  neovim  |  guitar  |  atrium  |
#   +----------+----------+----------+----------+----------+----------+
#   |                                                                 |
#   |                             atrium                              | 80%
#   |                                                                 |
#   +-----------------------------------------------------------------+
#
# The bottom row is cut first, so what the columns divide is the top strip
# alone rather than the whole window.
#
# `size` is what the NEW pane takes, so each column split hands the remainder
# rightward and the six come out equal: 5/6 of the window, then 4/5 of that,
# then 3/4, 2/3, 1/2 -- each split leaving exactly one column behind.
#
# `cwd` is relative to the worktree root, and the other five repos are bazzite's
# siblings under ~/projects/personal, hence `../name`. A worktree of this repo
# sits beside the main checkout too, so those stay pointed at the same places.
#
# Nothing is left without a command, so the cursor lands on the first pane --
# the bazzite column. The plan cannot ask for the atrium pane instead: the pane
# that opens the window is always the top one.

# name      from        split size  cwd          delay  command
g-bazzite   -           -     -     .            0      g
atrium      g-bazzite   v     80%   .            0      a
g-dotfiles  g-bazzite   h     83%   ../dotfiles  0      g
g-tmux      g-dotfiles  h     80%   ../tmux      0      g
g-neovim    g-tmux      h     75%   ../neovim    0      g
g-guitar    g-neovim    h     67%   ../guitar    0      g
g-atrium    g-guitar    h     50%   ../atrium    0      g
